 "text": "Assessor - Allamakee County, Iowa -->\nAssessor - Allamakee County, Iowa\nYou are using an outdated browser. Please upgrade your browser .\nMENU MENU\nDepartments\nAssessor\nAttorney\nAuditor\nConservation Board\nCounty Social Services\nEmergency Management\nE-911\nEngineer\nEnvironmental Health\nGIS\nPlanning and Development\nRecorder\nRelief\nSheriff’s Office\nSubstance Abuse\nTreasurer\nVeterans’ Affairs\nWaste Management\nBoards & Commissions\nBoard of Supervisors\nBoard of Health\nTownship Officials\nBoard / Commission Openings\nEmployment\nJob Opportunities\nEmployee FMLA Rights\nResources\nNews & Announcements\nCounty Documents\nEvents\nAbout\nContact\nSheriff\nDirectory\nSearch\nAssessor\n-->\nAssessor\nHome Departments Assessor\nWelcome to the Allamakee County Assessor's Office. It is our goal to provide information to the public about the duties of the assessor and various services offered by this office. We hope that you will find our website to be beneficial and informative.\nPROPERTY TAX SCAM/CLAIM ALERT:\nOur office is aware of a YouTube video claiming that Congress has changed property tax rules for homeowners born in the 1940s, 50s, or 60s. This claim is FALSE as it applies to Iowa. Congress has not created a nationwide property tax exemption, reduction, or freeze based on the decade a homeowner was born. Iowa property tax credits and exemptions are established by Iowa state law and have specific eligibility requirements. There is no new Iowa property tax benefit simply because you were born in a particular decade. For accurate information about Iowa property tax credits and exemptions, rely on the Iowa Department of Revenue or contact the Assessor's Office.\nREPORTING PROPERTY CHANGES:\nBuilding change forms are emailed (if we have an email on file) or mailed out each fall. You can find a copy of it here .\nOnline reporting can be completed here . Click on the search tab. Search by name or property address. Click on parcel ID number.\nClick the chat button icon on the tool bar below the search tab. Enter your changes in the comment box, click submit and you are done!\nPlease contact the Assessor's office with any questions.\nSALES QUESTIONNAIRE:\nDid you receive a postcard about completing a sales questionnaire and are wondering where to fill it out? Please visit the Beacon website here . Search for your property by name or address and click on the sales questionnaire link under the owner name on the parcel report.\nStaff\nKristy Roney\nAssessor\nEmail Assessor\nJonathan Luchsinger\nGIS Coordinator\nEmail GIS Coordinator\nToni Pearson\nChief Deputy Assessor\nEmail Chief Deputy Assessor\nAmanda Bloxham\nAppraiser\nEmail Appraiser\nClaire Opperman\nOffice Manager\nEmail Office Manager\nLocation\nAllamakee County Courthouse\n110 Allamakee St\nWaukon, Iowa 52172\nContact Us\nPhone: 563-568-3145\nFax: 563-568-0096\nEmail: Assessor\nOffice Hours\n8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m.\nDepartment Information\nGeneral Information about the Assessor\nInformation about what the Assessor's office duties are and important dates to remember.\nCredits and Exemptions\nInformation about the different types of credits and exemptions available for properties.\nAllamakee County Assessor Resources\nHomestead Exemption\nForms & Applications\n2025 Assessment Notice Explanation Letter\nEducational Resources\nAssessor’s Office Email Authorization\nForms & Applications\nIndustrial Property Tax Exemption\nForms & Applications\nIowa Barn & One Room Schoolhouse Exemption\nForms & Applications\nInformal Review Request\nForms & Applications\nGeothermal Tax Exemption\nForms & Applications\nPollution Control & Recycling Tax Exemption\nForms & Applications\nDisabled Veteran Homestead Tax Credit\nForms & Applications\nMilitary Tax Exemption\nForms & Applications\nPetition Board of Review Regular Session\nForms & Applications\nForest or Fruit Tree Reservation Exemption\nForms & Applications\nFamily Farm Tax Credit\nForms & Applications\nBuilding Change Form\nForms & Applications\nBoard of Review Procedural Rules\nEducational Resources\nHelpful Links\nProperty Search GIS - Beacon website to search for property.\nIowa Assessors - Property searches for all Iowa counties\nIowa State Association of Assessors\nIowa State Association of Counties\nIowa Department of Revenue\nCode of Iowa\nAll Assessor Documents\nEnglish ▼\nArabic Chinese (Simplified) Dutch English French German Italian Portuguese Russian Spanish\n110 Allamakee Street Waukon, IA 52172\nMon - Fri 8AM - 4PM\nPhone Directory\nCopyright © 2026 Allamakee County, Iowa. All Rights Reserved. Powered by Iroc Web Design Services .\nTop\n×\nSearch...",
